  "worked_solution": "Recall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -6 & 5 & -2 \\\\ 12 & -8 & 4\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-4{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $2$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2.\n$$",
